Each '''Glacite Mineshaft''' corresponds to a specific resource (e.g. {{Item|Umber}}, {{Item|Tungsten}}, {{Item|Ruby}}, etc), with some containing their respective resource's [[Gemstone Crystals|Gemstone Crystal]]. Most blocks inside '''Glacite Mineshafts''' can be broken, similar to the {{Zone|Crystal Hollows}}.

Upon opening a '''Glacite Mineshaft''', a portal will spawn, alongside the following dialogue:

{{Dialogue|&b&lMINESHAFT! &fA mineshaft portal spawned nearby!}}

Attempting to enter the '''Glacite Mineshaft''' will open the following interface:

{{:Glacite Mineshafts/UI}}

Players have {{Green|30s}} to enter a '''Glacite Mineshaft''' before it closes, if the player has entered a '''Glacite Mineshaft''' within the past {{Green|30s}}, they are prevented from joining the current instance and immediately despawn. Additionally, the player's pity does not increase for {{Green|1}} minute, if they're in the same [[Dwarven Mines]] lobby as before entering the Mineshaft.

=== Types ===
The base chance for each mineshaft type to spawn is {{Chance|5.88%|1|17|mineshafts}}. If the final block mined that leads to a mineshaft spawning matches one of the mineshaft types, it raises the chance for that mineshaft type to spawn to {{Chance|33.33%|1|3|mineshafts}}, and lowers the chance for others to {{Chance|4.17%|1|24|mineshafts}}.

If a gemstone mineshaft that is eligible for a crystal is chosen, there is a {{Chance|25%|1|4}} chance to get the crystal variant. This can be increased by {{Green|+0.5%}} per level using the [[Heart of the Mountain#Tier 10|Crystalline]] Heart of the Mountain perk, up to {{Green|+25.5%}} at level 51 (with {{Item|Blue Cheese Goblin Omelette}}). If a crystal variant does not spawn, the non-crystal variants have an equal chance to spawn. The {{code|_2}} variants generally have the biggest veins, followed by {{code|_1}}, and finally {{code|_C}}.

The [[Heart of the Mountain#Tier 10|Vanguard Seeker]] perk increases the weight of the Fairy mineshaft by {{Green|+1%}} per level, up to {{Green|+51%}} at level 51 (with {{Item|Blue Cheese Goblin Omelette}}) – bringing the chance to {{Chance|8.62%|1|11.6|mineshafts}}, and the chance for other mineshafts to {{Chance|5.71%|1|17.51|mineshafts}}. If an eligible block is mined, the chance for a matching mineshaft is {{Chance|33.33%|1|3|mineshafts}}, then the chance for a Fairy mineshaft is {{Chance|4.38%|1|22.84|mineshafts}}, and the chance for other mineshafts is {{Chance|3.81%|1|26.26|mineshafts}} each.

